{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"B\n    \n      Split Panel (IDE-style)\n      Left panel: cell list (compact, like tool list). Right panel: selected cell's args editor + result (reuses exact same layout as current ToolsTab execution panel). Feels like the existing Tools tab but with a cell list instead of a tool list.\n      \n        Notebook: \"Update Worker Language\"\n        \n          \n          \n            \n              CELLS\n              ▶ Run All\n            \n\n            \n              \n                findWorkerByEmail\n                ✓\n              \n              → worker\n            \n\n            \n              \n                getAssociateLanguages\n                ✓\n              \n              → languages\n            \n\n            \n              changeAssociateLanguage\n            \n\n            \n              + Add Cell\n            \n          \n\n          \n          \n            \n            \n              \n                \n                  findWorkerByEmail\n                  Arguments\n                \n                ▶ Execute\n              \n              \n                {\"\n                \"email\": \"{{ $.inputs.workerEmail }}\"\n                }\n              \n            \n            \n            \n              \n                Result\n                ✓ 230ms\n              \n              \n                { \"associateOID\": \"G3FEH...\", \"name\": { \"given\": \"Nithish\", ... } }\n              \n            \n          \n        \n      \n      \n        Pros\n          Directly reuses ToolsTab's args+results panel layout\n          More screen space for the active cell's editor\n          Consistent with existing Inspector UX patterns\n        \n        Cons\n          Can only see one cell at a time in detail\n          Less \"notebook\" feel — more like \"cell picker\"","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1776876586926}
{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"B\n    \n      Split Panel (IDE-style)\n      Left panel: cell list (compact, like tool list). Right panel: selected cell's args editor + result (reuses exact same layout as current ToolsTab execution panel). Feels like the existing Tools tab but with a cell list instead of a tool list.\n      \n        Notebook: \"Update Worker Language\"\n        \n          \n          \n            \n              CELLS\n              ▶ Run All\n            \n\n            \n              \n                findWorkerByEmail\n                ✓\n              \n              → worker\n            \n\n            \n              \n                getAssociateLanguages\n                ✓\n              \n              → languages\n            \n\n            \n              changeAssociateLanguage\n            \n\n            \n              + Add Cell\n            \n          \n\n          \n          \n            \n            \n              \n                \n                  findWorkerByEmail\n                  Arguments\n                \n                ▶ Execute\n              \n              \n                {\"\n                \"email\": \"{{ $.inputs.workerEmail }}\"\n                }\n              \n            \n            \n            \n              \n                Result\n                ✓ 230ms\n              \n              \n                { \"associateOID\": \"G3FEH...\", \"name\": { \"given\": \"Nithish\", ... } }\n              \n            \n          \n        \n      \n      \n        Pros\n          Directly reuses ToolsTab's args+results panel layout\n          More screen space for the active cell's editor\n          Consistent with existing Inspector UX patterns\n        \n        Cons\n          Can only see one cell at a time in detail\n          Less \"notebook\" feel — more like \"cell picker\"","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1776876595874}
